    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-a/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Prove by contradiction that for all real θ ( ) 5 cos θ + sin θ ≤ 2 .\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-a/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"√ Suppose, for a contradiction, that cos θ + sin θ &gt; 2 for some real θ. [B1] assumes the negation Both sides are positive under this assumption, so squaring preserves the inequality: (cos θ + sin θ)2 &gt; 2. Expanding the square gives cos2 θ + 2 cos θ sin θ + sin2 θ &gt; 2. [M1] squares and expands Replace cos2 θ + sin2 θ by 1 [A1] Pythagorean identity and 2 cos θ sin θ by sin 2θ. This gives 1 + sin 2θ &gt; 2, hence sin 2θ &gt; 1.\" style=\"--madas-width:536.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-a/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"[A1] double-angle identity For every real angle, sine is at most 1. √ This contradicts the assumption, so cos θ + sin θ ≤ 2 for all real θ. [A1] contradiction and conclusion\" style=\"--madas-width:445.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 5 marks.</p>"
