    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-a/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let y be the height in centimetres at time t minutes: Leakage makes the rate negative: With positive constant k, proportionality to the cube root of the height gives dy dt = −ky1/3. [B1] rate law Separate the variables: dy = −ky1/3 dt, hence dy/y1/3 = −k dt. [M1] separation Integrate both sides: 3 Z y−1/3 dy = Z 2y2/3 = −kt + C. −k dt, [M1] [A1] integration and constant\" style=\"--madas-width:497.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-a/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Multiplying by 2/3 gives y2/3 = At + B, where A = −2k/3 and B = 2C/3. At t = 0, y = 125; hence B = 1252/3 = 52 . = 25 [A1] initial height Now y2/3 = At + 25. At t = 3, y = 64, so 642/3 = 3A + 25. [A1] second condition Since 642/3 = 42 = 16, 16 = 3A + 25, −9 = 3A and A = −3. [A1] slope Thus y2/3 = 25 −3t, or y = (25 −3t)3/2 while there is water in the container: [A1] height model\" style=\"--madas-width:642.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-a/q11-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"At 7 minutes 35 seconds, t = 7 + 35/60 = 7 + 7/12 . [A1] time in minutes Then y2/3 = 25 −3(7 + 7/12) = 4 −7/4 . = 9/4 Raise both sides to the power 3/2: y = (9/4)3/2 = (3/2)3 = 27/8 cm\" style=\"--madas-width:418.7px\"></figure>",
